WEBVTT

00:05.650 --> 00:09.920
Hey there, third-rate stage directors. 
Finally showing your faces?

00:10.560 --> 00:13.540
Just can't stop interfering with us, can you?

00:13.540 --> 00:15.940
This time we'll show no mercy.

00:15.940 --> 00:17.670
We're in Ente Isla now.

00:17.670 --> 00:22.910
No way can you handle us in a world 
overflowing with celestial force!

00:22.910 --> 00:27.170
You oughta wait to say that stuff 
until you actually win, Raguel.

00:27.450 --> 00:29.930
It's just embarrassing if you lose later!

00:29.930 --> 00:34.680
I'm the demon boss—I'll go 
all-out mocking you for it.

00:34.680 --> 00:37.360
We'll find out soon enough.

00:37.360 --> 00:38.830
You gonna fight, too?

00:38.830 --> 00:42.430
Well, since you're asking... yeah.

00:42.760 --> 00:44.210
And you?

00:44.210 --> 00:46.950
Satan! Satan! Satan!

00:46.950 --> 00:48.440
Dunno why I asked.

00:48.440 --> 00:54.350
We have to rid Ente Isla of all the evil 
demons for the sake of Heaven's safety.

00:54.350 --> 00:56.700
I guess everything you do is third-rate.

00:57.050 --> 01:00.920
Miss Hero there already did that 
like ten minutes ago.

01:01.450 --> 01:05.530
If you're gonna rip off a blockbuster, try to
 do a <i>little</i> better than a B movie, losers!

01:05.530 --> 01:07.180
You're the same as ever.

01:10.370 --> 01:11.520
Alas Ramus.

01:11.520 --> 01:12.450
'Kay!

01:16.960 --> 01:19.430
I'm cool with you going against us,

01:19.430 --> 01:22.690
but what's your plan for <i>after</i> you betray 
humanity and side with Satan

01:22.690 --> 01:25.730
in front of so many witnesses?

01:26.730 --> 01:30.440
The more you talk, 
the more third-rate you sound.

01:30.440 --> 01:32.480
He may be an incurable perv,

01:32.480 --> 01:35.670
but at least Sariel is trying to get 
what he wants through his own merits.

01:35.670 --> 01:38.990
That makes him a thousand 
times better than you.

01:39.470 --> 01:43.500
Emi, you keep out of this. Just stay there.

01:46.320 --> 01:51.380
<i>My tiny hope almost spilled away</i>

01:51.380 --> 01:56.300
<i>I almost forgot the dream I had that day</i>

01:56.300 --> 02:04.080
<i>But you smiled, and it was 
enough to make me happy</i>

02:04.810 --> 02:06.890
<b>The Devil is a Part-Timer! Season 2</b>

02:07.180 --> 02:11.980
<i>Exhausted from lamenting the world</i>

02:11.980 --> 02:16.840
<i>I looked to the sky and saw it was blue</i>

02:16.840 --> 02:21.550
<i>I was still pretending to fight alone</i>

02:21.550 --> 02:26.620
<i>My nails cut into me as I clenched my fists</i>

02:26.620 --> 02:31.420
<i>Would life be easier if I just let go?</i>

02:31.420 --> 02:35.670
<i>I know I've got no intention of doing so</i>

02:35.670 --> 02:40.590
<i>My tiny hope almost spilled away</i>

02:40.590 --> 02:45.430
<i>I almost forgot the dream I had that day</i>

02:45.430 --> 02:53.110
<i>I'm still right here, still waiting for you</i>

02:55.320 --> 03:00.240
<i>I tried to stay quiet, but my voice rang out</i>

03:00.240 --> 03:05.240
<i>I sang the song I couldn't forget about</i>

03:05.240 --> 03:13.100
<i>I smiled with you, and 
that alone lightened my load</i>

03:16.750 --> 03:21.720
m 370 218 l 609 218 609 245 370 245

03:17.700 --> 03:21.200
This is Saint Aire. 
Which means that over there...

03:18.300 --> 03:21.720
<b>The Devil and the Hero Witness Change in Ente Isla</b>

03:18.300 --> 03:21.720
<b>The Devil and the Hero Witness Change in Ente Isla</b>

03:22.370 --> 03:23.220
Eme!

03:24.030 --> 03:25.100
Stop at once!

03:25.100 --> 03:28.680
This apostasy trial was 
entered into unlawfully.

03:28.680 --> 03:31.730
In the name of Crestia Bel, 
I call a halt to the proceedings!

03:31.730 --> 03:34.730
Al! Bel!

03:44.490 --> 03:45.740
Maou!

03:45.740 --> 03:47.700
I told you to stay there!

03:47.700 --> 03:49.410
You just protect your dad!

03:51.340 --> 03:53.010
Your Majesty, our location...

03:53.010 --> 03:53.740
Yeah.

04:01.910 --> 04:05.580
Satan! Satan! Satan! Satan! Satan!

04:06.170 --> 04:07.260
This isn't a good time!

04:07.260 --> 04:09.180
<i>You stupid Devil, what did you do?!</i>

04:09.560 --> 04:12.460
<i>Shut up! You guys were taking too long!</i>

04:12.460 --> 04:14.420
We've had trouble of our own.

04:14.420 --> 04:18.700
We managed to get back here with 
the good Emerada's angelic quill...

04:19.510 --> 04:24.450
But why is the army toppled like 
dominos in front of the Cloud Retreat?!

04:24.450 --> 04:26.530
Kill Satan! Kill, kill, kill, kill, kill!

04:26.530 --> 04:28.200
Some stuff happened.

04:26.530 --> 04:29.840
Kill, kill, kill, kill!

04:31.750 --> 04:33.310
But don't worry.

04:33.310 --> 04:37.000
I'll compensate you 
for the scooters I smashed up.

04:37.000 --> 04:39.890
You totaled them?! Those were mine!

04:39.890 --> 04:43.760
More importantly, 
the Emperor-Unifier was in here!

04:43.760 --> 04:47.300
That was Emilia's dad, 
and we already saved him!

04:47.300 --> 04:50.010
<i>Where is the Emperor, then?!</i>

04:50.010 --> 04:53.600
Stop playing around and keep 
your eyes on the fight, Satan!

05:00.440 --> 05:04.610
I've arranged for Libicocco to 
deliver the Emperor-Unifier to you.

05:04.610 --> 05:05.950
He's in your hands.

05:05.950 --> 05:06.840
What?

05:06.840 --> 05:10.790
Alciel? What's this about? 
I don't understand you!

05:17.770 --> 05:19.620
I think I have to go...

05:22.150 --> 05:23.460
Hey, isn't that...?

05:24.270 --> 05:26.050
H-Hey, what are you doing?!

05:26.050 --> 05:29.560
It <i>is</i> a shard of Yesod! 
That's what we needed!

05:31.700 --> 05:36.940
Aw, but this one's no good. It's been 
exposed to too much celestial force.

05:42.660 --> 05:44.220
Does this mean...

05:44.650 --> 05:47.110
Alciel has one, too?

05:49.280 --> 05:51.020
Chamuel, time to call them.

05:55.040 --> 05:56.290
Watch out!

05:56.290 --> 05:58.170
A Heavenly Regiment is headed your way!

05:58.170 --> 05:59.670
Damn.

06:03.430 --> 06:04.870
Light of Iron!

06:05.620 --> 06:08.300
I don't understand, but I shall assist!

06:16.060 --> 06:17.290
Ashiya!

06:17.290 --> 06:18.310
I am fine.

06:19.200 --> 06:22.290
I'm not sure I understand, 
but are you saying you'll be okay

06:22.290 --> 06:25.840
with a shard exposed to magic 
instead of celestial force?

06:25.840 --> 06:28.680
Yep! I think that would work!

06:28.680 --> 06:29.810
Wait here.

06:35.800 --> 06:37.010
Emilia, what are you doing?

06:37.010 --> 06:39.080
Just keep quiet!

06:39.820 --> 06:40.830
That's—

06:43.090 --> 06:44.090
Satan!

06:44.590 --> 06:45.830
Uh, okay?

06:45.830 --> 06:46.840
Maou!

06:47.840 --> 06:49.590
Hey! What are you doing?!

06:49.970 --> 06:54.350
Yeah, "knowing" requires the head.

06:57.950 --> 06:59.410
Your Majesty?

06:59.410 --> 07:00.890
Thank you, Emi.

07:02.250 --> 07:05.740
This Yesod shard has been 
exposed to magic for a long time.

07:05.740 --> 07:09.010
Seems like that made it easier 
for Acieth to adapt to me.

07:09.010 --> 07:10.650
Heh heh heh!

07:18.090 --> 07:19.970
Time to get them, Maou!

07:19.970 --> 07:20.840
Yeah!

07:27.460 --> 07:29.250
Better Half?

07:29.250 --> 07:31.220
I'm pissed off.

07:31.220 --> 07:34.420
At you guys, for bullying 
and abusing my comrades,

07:34.420 --> 07:39.060
my subordinates, my citizens, 
and the humans I plan to rule.

07:39.060 --> 07:43.540
Today I'm showin' no mercy!

07:43.540 --> 07:46.470
I'll say the same right back to you.

07:46.470 --> 07:49.110
Satan, today I kill you!

07:49.110 --> 07:53.060
Shut up! Prepare to go down, 
you goddamn angels!

07:55.910 --> 07:58.110
Another sacred sword?

07:58.110 --> 08:00.630
Acieth's my little sister.

08:00.630 --> 08:01.820
Little sister?

08:03.280 --> 08:07.040
Yep! The other half of Yesod!

08:07.040 --> 08:08.560
"Other half"...

08:08.560 --> 08:11.930
B-But isn't that a sacred sword? 
Why can he use it?

08:12.260 --> 08:14.300
Why does it radiate magic?

08:14.300 --> 08:19.590
It would seem that not all Yesod 
shards are celestial force-based.

08:20.430 --> 08:25.660
I believe we've labored under a grave
misapprehension about what the sephiroth are.

08:26.030 --> 08:28.300
Neither your sword with Alas Ramus

08:28.300 --> 08:32.700
nor His Majesty's sword 
with that girl are "sacred."

08:32.700 --> 08:37.900
Yesod is branches. They tie 
life and life, heart and heart.

08:37.900 --> 08:40.970
I was always with Acieth.

08:40.970 --> 08:43.120
Branches that connect hearts?

08:43.570 --> 08:46.250
Go, Papa!

08:48.290 --> 08:51.620
H-How could a sacred sword do that?

08:51.620 --> 08:54.860
I'm glad to see you 
in good health, Father Olba.

08:55.510 --> 09:01.720
I didn't expect to see you in Efzahan after 
you went missing in the world of Japan.

09:01.720 --> 09:03.640
<i>You</i>.

09:04.390 --> 09:08.370
Sadly, I cannot take the time to rejoice 
in this reunion, respected Father.

09:08.370 --> 09:12.680
It is my duty to judge you for your sins.

09:12.680 --> 09:16.350
Malebranche leaders, in this moment alone,

09:16.350 --> 09:19.830
I issue you an order 
as Demon General Crestia Bel

09:19.830 --> 09:21.420
of the new Devil's army.

09:21.930 --> 09:25.070
What? "Demon General"?

09:25.070 --> 09:27.130
Farfa, what's going on?

09:27.130 --> 09:28.800
Hold, Barbariccia.

09:29.200 --> 09:32.300
What order do you intend to give?

09:34.120 --> 09:37.150
Quietly go along with everything 
that's about to happen.

09:37.150 --> 09:40.550
If you do, King Satan will 
forgive your unauthorized actions

09:40.550 --> 09:43.650
and allow you to return to the good Camio.

09:43.650 --> 09:47.120
You know Camio, human?

09:47.120 --> 09:51.570
Very well. We shall obey you, new general.

09:52.570 --> 09:56.320
It is too late for us to make 
excuses for our foolishness.

09:56.780 --> 10:00.870
We allowed ourselves to be deceived and 
betrayed by Olba and those from Heaven,

10:00.870 --> 10:02.980
and lost many of our brethren.

10:02.980 --> 10:05.190
We must face the consequences.

10:05.190 --> 10:08.580
Wh-What is the meaning of this?!

10:08.580 --> 10:13.070
What I wish for has not changed 
since we met, Father Olba.

10:13.070 --> 10:15.640
All I want is to build a world 
where all our people

10:15.640 --> 10:20.310
walk in the light of faith, 
filled with justice and safety.

10:20.640 --> 10:25.620
In Japan, I gained the strength of heart 
to work toward that world.

10:25.620 --> 10:27.350
That's the only thing that changed.

10:27.350 --> 10:29.970
Those are genuine angels.

10:29.970 --> 10:33.570
Do you intend to betray 
both Heaven and Ente Isla,

10:33.570 --> 10:36.490
and remain allied with 
the Devil along with Emilia?

10:37.170 --> 10:41.560
I never thought I'd hear such 
words from you, Father Olba.

10:42.530 --> 10:46.620
There can be no <i>genuine</i> <i>angels</i> in this world.

10:48.450 --> 10:53.380
They may call themselves Gabriel, Chamuel,
and Raguel, but they are ordinary humans!

10:53.380 --> 10:58.090
If powerful people who grow wings 
get to declare themselves angels,

10:58.090 --> 11:04.080
then I'll go buy costume wings at Tokyo 
Hand and call myself an angel, too.

11:06.110 --> 11:09.380
Eight Scarves knights who 
volunteered to fight for justice,

11:09.380 --> 11:11.390
I understand your bewilderment.

11:11.390 --> 11:13.860
Still, everything I've said is true.

11:13.860 --> 11:17.150
As I speak, two heroes 
with sacred swords in hand

11:17.150 --> 11:20.520
are punishing the demons who have 
brought a second age of terror

11:20.520 --> 11:24.410
upon your great empire, 
your beloved Efzahan!

11:24.410 --> 11:25.650
What?

11:25.650 --> 11:26.910
"Demons"?

11:27.300 --> 11:29.310
Bel, what are you playing at?

11:29.310 --> 11:34.420
It was not Alciel or the Malebranche 
who brought this chaos to Efzahan.

11:34.810 --> 11:40.020
I'm sure the sovereign of this great nation, 
the Emperor-Unifier, will provide proof.

11:42.490 --> 11:44.430
His Majesty!

11:46.290 --> 11:50.410
Hi, Olba! You're lookin' good. 
Long time no see!

11:50.410 --> 11:51.940
A-Albert...

11:55.060 --> 11:59.320
All right, everyone, your attention, please!

12:00.830 --> 12:09.080
Everything... she says... is true.

12:09.450 --> 12:15.270
Alciel... in fact protected me...

12:16.150 --> 12:20.890
and endeavored to keep... 
my brave and loyal knights...

12:20.890 --> 12:25.310
from tragically harming each other.

12:27.190 --> 12:30.600
Do not mistake our enemy.

12:30.600 --> 12:33.900
Gather under the sacred sword.

12:33.900 --> 12:39.380
Show the heavens... our nation's might.

12:39.380 --> 12:41.360
Yes, Sire!

12:42.230 --> 12:44.930
Your Great and August Majesty,

12:44.930 --> 12:49.370
Crestia Bel, lead investigator of the Grand 
Hoshin Church's Doctrinal Correction Council

12:49.370 --> 12:53.540
has heard your words, and 
so has High Priest Olba.

12:53.540 --> 12:55.790
Bel, how dare you!

12:55.790 --> 13:00.250
I dunno what your ambition is, 
but this is game, set, and match.

13:00.970 --> 13:03.930
You didn't live like a human, 
but try to die like one.

13:06.030 --> 13:08.680
As the Doctrinal Correction 
Council's highest inquisitor,

13:08.680 --> 13:10.420
I hereby deliver this verdict:

13:10.420 --> 13:14.900
Fellow humans, our true enemy is the enemy 
of those wielding the sacred swords.

13:15.240 --> 13:18.140
The three apostates 
calling themselves angels!

13:18.140 --> 13:19.650
Papa!

13:20.080 --> 13:24.860
Papa's gonna work even harder than 
usual—my daughter is watching!

13:29.730 --> 13:35.430
Satan, Satan, Satan, Satan, Satan, Satan!

13:31.070 --> 13:35.080
You need to chill out, Chamuel, 
or we're about to be in trouble.

13:35.430 --> 13:39.840
Kill Satan! Kill Satan! Kill Satan!

13:45.420 --> 13:46.930
No getting away!

13:46.930 --> 13:48.800
Whoa, there. I won't let you pass.

13:56.440 --> 13:58.620
W-Well, that's not very nice!

13:58.620 --> 14:04.440
I gave you so much info, I thought 
you'd pull your punches a little.

14:04.440 --> 14:06.600
Get real!

14:06.600 --> 14:10.510
This <i>is</i> me pulling my punches—
I'm not killing you on the spot.

14:10.880 --> 14:15.460
I'm bringing you back to Japan and 
making you spill everything you know!

14:16.810 --> 14:21.710
Goodness, what a mess this all is.

14:21.710 --> 14:26.370
Emerada, weren't you on trial 
by the Church or something?

14:26.370 --> 14:29.720
Al and Bel rescued me!

14:29.720 --> 14:32.720
It put us behind schedule a bit, though.

14:32.970 --> 14:39.730
Yes, we were giving a little spanking to 
some rats who'd been nesting in the Church.

14:40.260 --> 14:41.480
Eme...

14:41.480 --> 14:48.940
Emilia, fight for your own sake 
from now on and not for the world's.

14:48.940 --> 14:52.090
Al and I will support you 
with all we've got,

14:52.090 --> 14:54.490
like we always have.

14:55.100 --> 14:56.270
Human.

14:56.820 --> 15:01.070
I don't know what you intend 
to do next... but don't die.

15:01.070 --> 15:03.260
I pray that by the next time we meet,

15:03.260 --> 15:07.130
we'll be on speaking terms 
instead of fighting terms.

15:07.130 --> 15:13.260
Yeah, right. Not a single one 
of you humans makes sense.

15:13.780 --> 15:15.400
Nor do you.

15:16.640 --> 15:21.200
Lately I feel as though 
I don't understand demons at all.

15:24.270 --> 15:26.060
Hey, listen.

15:26.060 --> 15:26.940
Yeah?

15:26.940 --> 15:30.960
I owe you an apology for something.

15:30.960 --> 15:33.170
Is this about the Malebranche?

15:33.170 --> 15:38.410
Yes. I don't have the right 
anymore to blame you for—

15:38.410 --> 15:41.290
You've been worrying 
about that? That's dumb.

15:42.680 --> 15:45.490
You can't let a thing like that shake you.

15:45.490 --> 15:49.840
You did it because you're the Hero, 
and I caused it because I'm the Devil.

15:49.840 --> 15:52.400
Don't try to make it more
complicated than that.

15:56.970 --> 16:00.540
Nothing about our relationship has changed.

16:01.020 --> 16:06.000
Besides, you owe bigger apologies 
to other people right now:

16:06.000 --> 16:07.850
Chi and Rika Suzuki.

16:08.980 --> 16:13.680
Oh, FYI, I already bought a present for Chi.

16:13.680 --> 16:15.970
I doubt you got anything, right?

16:15.970 --> 16:19.490
And Chi's already feeling down!

16:23.870 --> 16:28.250
Seriously, what's wrong with you? 
Whatever you ate made you <i>really</i> sick.

16:30.080 --> 16:32.980
Well, I guess that shows 
how rough you've had it.

16:32.980 --> 16:37.940
When we get back to Japan, just apologize
 and tell them all about it.

16:37.940 --> 16:41.270
They're your friends, yeah? 
They'll understand.

16:42.900 --> 16:43.900
Yeah.

17:02.010 --> 17:03.040
Mr. Maou!

17:03.420 --> 17:05.590
Wow, Chi, that was fast.

17:05.590 --> 17:06.520
Chiho!

17:06.520 --> 17:07.790
Chi-sis!

17:08.590 --> 17:09.790
Miss Yusa!

17:10.740 --> 17:12.460
We're home, Chi.

17:12.460 --> 17:14.720
I'm so glad you're okay.

17:14.720 --> 17:18.830
I'm really, really glad!

17:18.830 --> 17:21.050
I'm sorry I worried you.

17:21.050 --> 17:24.320
Chi-sis, no crying.

17:24.320 --> 17:25.950
Alas Ramus...

17:32.270 --> 17:34.070
Welcome home!

17:38.980 --> 17:41.390
Here you go. It's nice and cold!

17:41.390 --> 17:43.020
Thanks, Chi.

17:43.020 --> 17:44.580
Fank you!

17:44.580 --> 17:46.030
Thank you very much.

17:46.030 --> 17:47.460
My thanks.

17:49.790 --> 17:52.290
Tiny or not, it's good to be back here.

17:53.040 --> 17:56.850
I'm so hungry! Isn't there anything to eat?

17:56.850 --> 17:58.490
Learn some manners.

17:59.160 --> 18:02.310
Urushihara, did anything happen 
while we were away?

18:02.310 --> 18:03.850
Nope.

18:05.040 --> 18:08.820
At least you apparently learned to make 
new tea when you finish the pitcher.

18:10.280 --> 18:11.230
Yes?

18:12.010 --> 18:13.480
Good day.

18:14.480 --> 18:17.390
Landlady! And Ms. Amane!

18:17.390 --> 18:20.240
Welcome back, everyone. Glad you're okay.

18:20.600 --> 18:27.690
Mr. Ashiya, may I trouble you to carry 
this handsome young man to my home?

18:27.690 --> 18:30.000
Y-Yes, ma'am, I will!

18:30.000 --> 18:31.250
Where's Nord?

18:31.250 --> 18:34.090
I've put him in an empty room downstairs.

18:34.090 --> 18:36.780
I don't believe he's awake yet.

18:36.780 --> 18:38.630
Yusa is with him.

18:38.980 --> 18:41.140
And someone else, too.

18:46.390 --> 18:48.200
Yo, good to see ya.

18:48.200 --> 18:49.340
Rika...

18:49.640 --> 18:51.210
E-Er—

18:51.210 --> 18:54.200
Hold on, I want to say something first.

18:56.030 --> 19:00.070
I have good news and bad news. 
Which do you want first?

19:00.070 --> 19:02.170
I've always wanted to say that!

19:02.170 --> 19:05.630
Um, okay, I'll take the bad news.

19:05.630 --> 19:06.680
Okay.

19:07.210 --> 19:10.160
Sorry, but you're fired.

19:10.160 --> 19:12.660
The floor leader went to bat for you,

19:12.660 --> 19:16.670
but there was no defending a month 
of radio silence and unexcused absence.

19:16.670 --> 19:19.830
I see... Well, it makes sense.

19:19.830 --> 19:23.310
So, about the good news...

19:23.310 --> 19:25.550
Hmm? R-Right.

19:25.930 --> 19:29.910
I'm giving you the right to choose 
what I call you from now on,

19:29.910 --> 19:31.310
Miss Emilia Justina.

19:34.930 --> 19:37.690
Rika, I...

19:38.200 --> 19:40.950
Hey, it's no fair for you to cry!

19:40.950 --> 19:44.590
Really scary stuff happened 
to me because of you,

19:44.590 --> 19:46.450
so you should let <i>me</i> cry!

19:46.450 --> 19:50.080
I cried a ton, actually. It was super scary!

19:51.590 --> 19:55.130
But you know, if there's 
anything I'd want an apology for,

19:55.130 --> 19:57.760
that's honestly the only thing.

20:00.010 --> 20:01.410
Did I ever tell you

20:01.410 --> 20:04.340
that I swam at the National 
Athletic Meet back in high school?

20:04.340 --> 20:07.290
"M-Meet"? No, I don't know that story...

20:07.290 --> 20:10.100
I lost in the prelims, though.

20:10.100 --> 20:15.350
Also, the other kids called me 
"Rika-bug" all through in middle school.

20:15.350 --> 20:19.000
I always thought it wasn't nice 
to put "bug" in a girl's nickname.

20:20.880 --> 20:24.280
We don't get many chances to 
learn about a friend's past

20:24.280 --> 20:26.370
unless they specifically 
tell their life story.

20:26.690 --> 20:31.310
Your backstory just happens to 
be a little unusual, that's all.

20:31.980 --> 20:33.370
Rika...

20:34.210 --> 20:38.290
What's important to me is that 
we can chitchat and be ourselves,

20:38.290 --> 20:40.630
and that we get tea together 
after work sometimes.

20:40.630 --> 20:44.970
Well, things aren't looking great 
on that front since you're fired now, but...

20:46.890 --> 20:51.640
Basically, that's all you have to do 
to keep being friends with me.

20:52.210 --> 20:54.920
Anything more is kind of a bonus.

20:56.050 --> 20:57.040
Okay...

20:57.800 --> 20:58.650
Okay!

20:58.650 --> 21:02.650
Hey! No crying! That's the
 one thing I won't allow!

21:03.250 --> 21:05.940
Your dad hasn't woken up yet, right?

21:05.940 --> 21:08.910
Save your tears for the touching reunion.

21:09.340 --> 21:14.330
You did good making it this far. 
I hope your dad gets well soon.

21:18.890 --> 21:20.170
Emilia...

21:20.170 --> 21:21.640
Dad!

21:23.280 --> 21:26.180
Is this a dream?

21:26.180 --> 21:29.730
No, it's not a dream. It's really not!

21:29.730 --> 21:31.180
Dad...

21:31.180 --> 21:32.930
Dad!

21:37.980 --> 21:41.910
It's been while since we all sat 
around the dinner tables together, huh?

21:41.910 --> 21:43.820
It's so crowded...

21:43.820 --> 21:47.660
Why not put the clutter in the closet?

21:47.660 --> 21:49.200
Clutter?

21:49.200 --> 21:51.130
Why me?

21:52.790 --> 21:54.080
Urushihara!

21:54.080 --> 21:56.830
You binge-shopped while we were away again!

21:56.830 --> 21:59.080
More importantly, do something about her!

21:56.830 --> 21:59.690
We'll just call this a reception service event.

21:59.690 --> 22:01.960
With chilled tofu and ginger bud 
for the main dish.

22:01.960 --> 22:04.260
Tofu! Ginger bud!

22:04.260 --> 22:05.970
Enough with that!

22:18.070 --> 22:24.230
<i>I woke up, saw the hurrying 
second hand on the clock</i>

22:24.230 --> 22:30.990
<i>And murmured "Slow down a little," 
in case it would help</i>

22:32.280 --> 22:38.370
<i>This world that's a colorful mix of hues</i>

22:38.370 --> 22:46.460
<i>And this feeling that 
will never wither or change</i>

22:46.460 --> 22:49.800
<i>Nostalgia (I don't know why)</i>

22:49.800 --> 22:53.470
<i>Collecting matching shards 
(but somehow I can tell)</i>

22:53.470 --> 22:56.350
<i>I can become (I want to protect you)</i>

22:56.350 --> 23:02.610
<i>The sun or the moon to light you up</i>

23:03.020 --> 23:07.410
<i>Look how it sparkles, bloomin'</i>

23:07.410 --> 23:10.120
<i>It's so bright that a smile</i>

23:10.120 --> 23:14.080
<i>Blooms on my face again today</i>

23:14.080 --> 23:17.290
<i>As my cheeks blaze</i>

23:17.290 --> 23:21.550
<i>Petals flutter on the wind, bloomin'</i>

23:21.550 --> 23:25.040
<i>Embrace me as I cry</i>

23:25.040 --> 23:32.050
<i>The teardrops in my eyes reflect it all</i>

23:32.050 --> 23:37.810
<i>There you are</i>
